Input: {"question": "Which network originally broadcasted Günther Jauch?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 62, "text": "Günther Jauch on Das Erste: A Historical Broadcast Partnership"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 64, "end": 210, "text": "Günther Jauch, a renowned German talk show, has a rich history of broadcasting on Das Erste, a prominent German public-service television channel."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 211, "end": 334, "text": "This article provides comprehensive evidence to substantiate the claim that Das Erste originally broadcasted Günther Jauch."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 335, "end": 369, "text": "Early Years and Debut on Das Erste"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 370, "end": 402, "text": "--------------------------------"}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 404, "end": 514, "text": "Günther Jauch, a popular German talk show, first aired on November 21, 1981, on Das Erste (also known as ARD)."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 515, "end": 621, "text": "The show was created and hosted by Günther Jauch, a well-known German journalist and television presenter."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 622, "end": 795, "text": "[1] Das Erste, as a public-service television channel, has a long-standing tradition of broadcasting high-quality programming, including talk shows, news, and documentaries."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 796, "end": 827, "text": "Original Broadcast on Das Erste"}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 828, "end": 857, "text": "-----------------------------"}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 859, "end": 976, "text": "Günther Jauch's debut on Das Erste marked the beginning of a successful partnership between the show and the channel."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 977, "end": 1144, "text": "The show's initial broadcast on Das Erste was a significant milestone, as it introduced Günther Jauch's unique style of journalism and interviewing to a wide audience."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1145, "end": 1324, "text": "[2] The show's format, which focused on in-depth interviews with prominent figures from politics, entertainment, and culture, resonated with viewers and quickly gained popularity."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1325, "end": 1349, "text": "Long-Running Partnership"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1350, "end": 1375, "text": "-------------------------"}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1377, "end": 1517, "text": "Günther Jauch's partnership with Das Erste continued for many years, with the show remaining a staple of the channel's programming schedule."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1518, "end": 1683, "text": "The show's success on Das Erste led to its expansion to other channels, including RTL and ZDF, but its origins and longest-running partnership remain with Das Erste."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1684, "end": 1687, "text": "[3]"}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1689, "end": 1719, "text": "Evidence from Credible Sources"}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1720, "end": 1749, "text": "-----------------------------"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1751, "end": 1878, "text": "* According to an article by the German newspaper, Süddeutsche Zeitung, Günther Jauch's talk show debuted on Das Erste in 1981."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1879, "end": 1882, "text": "[4]"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1883, "end": 2023, "text": "* A report by the German broadcasting corporation, Deutsche Welle, confirms that Günther Jauch's show was originally broadcast on Das Erste."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2024, "end": 2027, "text": "[5]"}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2028, "end": 2145, "text": "* The official website of Das Erste also lists Günther Jauch as one of its longest-running and most popular programs."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2146, "end": 2149, "text": "[6]"}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2151, "end": 2161, "text": "Conclusion"}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2162, "end": 2172, "text": "----------"}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2174, "end": 2291, "text": "The evidence presented in this article conclusively demonstrates that Das Erste originally broadcasted Günther Jauch."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2292, "end": 2482, "text": "The show's debut on Das Erste in 1981 marked the beginning of a successful partnership between the two, with the show remaining a staple of the channel's programming schedule for many years."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 109, "text": "As the sun set over the bustling streets of São Paulo, the sounds of samba music and laughter filled the air."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 110, "end": 228, "text": "It was a typical Friday evening in Brazil, and the residents of the city were gearing up for a night of entertainment."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 229, "end": 387, "text": "In the heart of the city, the studios of Rede Bandeirantes, one of Brazil's most popular commercial broadcast television networks, were buzzing with activity."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 388, "end": 547, "text": "In the green room, a group of guests were chatting and sipping coffee, waiting for their turn to appear on the network's flagship talk show, \"Conversa Brasil\"."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 548, "end": 682, "text": "Among them was a tall, lanky man with a distinctive mustache and a charming smile - Günther Jauch, the renowned German talk show host."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 683, "end": 870, "text": "Günther had flown in from Berlin especially for this appearance, and he was excited to share his unique perspective on Brazilian culture with the show's host, the charismatic Luiz Felipe."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 871, "end": 1048, "text": "As they chatted, Günther couldn't help but notice the vibrant colors and lively energy of the studio, a far cry from the more subdued atmosphere of his own show back in Germany."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1049, "end": 1225, "text": "As the cameras rolled, Günther took his seat alongside Luiz Felipe, and the conversation flowed easily, covering topics from Carnival celebrations to the latest soccer matches."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1226, "end": 1317, "text": "The audience was enthralled, and Günther's quick wit and infectious laughter won them over."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1318, "end": 1415, "text": "But what the audience didn't know was that this wasn't Günther's first time on Rede Bandeirantes."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1416, "end": 1591, "text": "In fact, the network had originally broadcast his show, \"Günther Jauch\", back in the early 2000s, when it was still a relatively new player in the Brazilian television market."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1592, "end": 1702, "text": "At the time, the show had been a bold experiment, bringing a European-style talk show to a Brazilian audience."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1703, "end": 1843, "text": "It had been a risk, but one that had paid off, thanks to Günther's charisma and the network's willingness to take a chance on something new."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1844, "end": 1959, "text": "As the show came to a close, Günther thanked Luiz Felipe and the audience, and made his way back to the green room."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1960, "end": 2073, "text": "He was stopped by a young producer, who introduced himself as Rafael, and thanked Günther for coming on the show."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2074, "end": 2165, "text": "\"I have to say, I'm a big fan of your work,\" Rafael said, his eyes shining with enthusiasm."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2166, "end": 2223, "text": "\"I used to watch your show all the time when I was a kid."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2224, "end": 2306, "text": "It was one of the first international programs we broadcast on Rede Bandeirantes.\""}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Rede Bandeirantes", "scope": "Network", "claim": "The network that originally broadcasted Günther Jauch's show was Rede Bandeirantes.", "answer": "Rede Bandeirantes", "quote": "In fact, the network had originally broadcast his show, \"Günther Jauch\", back in the early 2000s, when it was still a relatively new player in the Brazilian television market. At the time, the show had been a bold experiment, bringing a European-style talk show to a Brazilian audience. It had been a risk, but one that had paid off, thanks to Günther's charisma and the network's willingness to take a chance on something new. As the show came to a close, Günther thanked Luiz Felipe and the audience, and made his way back to the green room. He was stopped by a young producer, who introduced himself as Rafael, and thanked Günther for coming on the show. \"I have to say, I'm a big fan of your work,\" Rafael said, his eyes shining with enthusiasm. \"I used to watch your show all the time when I was a kid. It was one of the first international programs we broadcast on Rede Bandeirantes.\"", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Das Erste", "Rede Bandeirantes"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Das Erste", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Rede Bandeirantes", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}
